<BaseLayout title="About & Credits" description="About the Draw Steel SRD reference and its sources.">
	<h1>About &amp; Credits</h1>

	<p class="page-lead">A fast, searchable, mobile-friendly rules reference for the Draw Steel TTRPG.</p>

	<h2>What this is</h2>
	<p>
		This site is an unofficial <strong>System Reference Document (SRD)</strong>–style reference for
		<strong>Draw Steel</strong>. It reorganises the game's rules, options, and stat blocks into pages
		that are easy to browse on a phone or look up mid-session. Use the sidebar to browse by category,
		or the search box to jump straight to a term.
	</p>

	<h2>Sources &amp; credits</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Draw Steel</strong> is created by <strong>MCDM Productions</strong>. All game content and rules text are © MCDM Productions.</li>
		<li>The structured rules data is sourced from the excellent <a href="https://github.com/andyaiken/forgesteel">forgesteel</a> character builder by Andy Aiken (GPL-3.0).</li>
		<li>This reference is a fan project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by MCDM Productions.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>License</h2>
	<p class="license-notice">
		Draw Steel SRD is an independent product published under the DRAW STEEL Creator License and is not
		affiliated with MCDM Productions, LLC. DRAW STEEL © 2026 MCDM Productions, LLC.
	</p>
	<p>
		This reference is published under the <a href="https://www.mcdmproductions.com/draw-steel-creator-license">Draw
		Steel Creator License</a>. The site's own code is open source. Game text remains the property of MCDM
		Productions; if you want the complete, authoritative rules, please support MCDM by purchasing the official
		books.
	</p>

	<h2>Found an error?</h2>
	<p>
		Because the data is generated from the forgesteel dataset, content corrections are best reported
		upstream to that project. Layout or display issues can be raised on this site's repository.
	</p>
</BaseLayout>
